{"study_accession":"PRJNA796355","secondary_study_accession":"SRP354565","title":"Next Generation Sequencing of human circulating neutrophils treated with decidual explant supernatant or not","description":"Decidual microenvironment can induce circulating neutrophils to acquire the phenotypes and functions of decidual polymorphonuclear myeloid-derived suppressor cell (PMN-MDSCs). The mechanism of PMN-MDSCs differentiation induced by decidual microenvironment has not been fully understood. Here we performed whole genome expression profile of neutrophils treated with decidual explant supernatant (DES) or not (n=3). Total RNA were extracted. Transcriptome libraries were generated with the Illumina TruseqTM RNA sample prep Kit, and sequencing was performed on the Illumina Novaseq 6000 platform. There were differences of gene expression after DES treatment. Overall design: Retinal mRNA profiles of human circulating neutrophils treated with decidual explant supernatant or not (n=3).","pubmed":"35664000","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN24849169","study_accession":"PRJNA796355","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"DES_C","description":"DES_C","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM5808439","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-05-15","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood, circulating neutrophils"],["years","26 years"],["tissue","blood"],["sex","female"],["treatment","decidual explant supernatant (DES)"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR17562541","experiment_accession":"SRX13731813","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":29118903,"base_count":8793908706,"first_public":"2022-05-15","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM5808439: DES_C Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN24849170","study_accession":"PRJNA796355","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"DES_